		{
			"id":"d674df2c9c1b6ed7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Theories\n\n- The Black Key is lying with the last King of Eight\n\t- The Black Key is lying in the tomb of the King of Orinda?\n- In Aries Court where the King now lays\n\t- The place I am is the Orinda Aries Court?\n- A patient figure a reckoning great\n\t- Maybe the art representing the old man waiting?\n\t- Or maybe I need to be patient as the old man waiting by the chair\n\t- Maybe related to the many photos with people sitting on chairs\n- On the sacred hour that timeworn phrase\n\t- I should come at 1:30\n\t- What phrase?\n\t\t- Ovinn Nevarei?\n\t\t\t- Not really\n- A sullen cross as five stars align\n\t- The day needs to be have a Southern Cross Constellation\n\t\t- Unsure if I need to activate the constellation in the Observatory or just have the Stars that would have the constellations in the sky\n- Will a youth approach with empty arms\n\t- I should have no items in my inventory?\n- Without gifts nor gold nor mannered charms\n\t- I should have no gold, maybe gems, dies and keys?\n- And in sky above a brilliant sign\n\t- ~~I should come during the night?~~\n\t- It works if you do this on the day\n\nMaybe with this Black Key I can interact with the Black Mirror?\n\nI wonder if there are more conditions.\n- ~~Maybe changing the Secret Garden Relic to the Orindia Symbol (South)~~\n- ~~Maybe changing the Secret Garden Relic to the Moon Symbol (North)~~\n- ~~Maybe I shouldn't wait in the Court, but somewhere instead with the symbol?~~\n\nThe conditions listed are correct.\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1740,
			"y":1200,
			"width":660,
			"height":1070,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{"id":"f84140bc6de96967","type":"file","file":"99. attachments/BLUE_PRINCE_nynCbTGPe5.png","x":340,"y":3180,"width":1200,"height":675},
		{
			"id":"94ceacbcee9419ba",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Clock Puzzle Theories\n- The Museum Map timestamps\n\t- Did not work\n- The dates on seven of the Red Letters do not work\n\t- Did not work\n- Test 10/05, 10/06 based on the History of Orindia book telling about the day that the King Desilets III died\n\t- 10/05 and 10/06 did not work\n\t- 11/05 and 11/06 also did not work (Herbert death)\n- Maybe because there are six rows with 3 squares, it means that the solution is 6 numbers made of 3 numerals.\n\t- This means the number goes from 01:00 to 09:59\n- There is a chance that\n\t- Number three is 5--\n\t- Number four is -0-\n\t- Number five is -0-\n\t- Number six is  --7\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-260,
			"y":3180,
			"width":560,
			"height":675
		},
